course: dictionary
lesson: 12864
title: Enlarged: made bigger
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Enlarged» comes from the verb «enlarge», which means to make something bigger. The «-ed» ending shows it happened in the past: «We enlarged the picture» means we made the picture bigger.
explain: As an adjective, «enlarged» describes something that has already been made bigger. «An enlarged photo» is a photo that has been printed larger than the first copy. Ask yourself: what was made bigger? The clue is the word before it.
explain: In maths, an enlarged shape keeps the same angles but has longer sides. «Enlarged by a scale factor of 2» means each side is twice as long. In medicine, «an enlarged heart» means the heart is bigger than normal, often because of illness, so the word can be about health too.
fact: Enlarge means to make something bigger.
fact: «Enlarged» can mean made bigger, as in «We enlarged the picture.»
fact: «An enlarged photo» is a photo that has been printed larger.
fact: In maths, an enlarged shape keeps the same angles, but its sides are longer; the scale factor tells you how many times bigger.
fact: In medicine, «an enlarged heart» means the heart is bigger than normal, often because of illness.
exercise: «The photo was enlarged so we could see Grandma's smile.» What does enlarged mean here? | *Made bigger | Taken in the dark | Made smaller | Lost
exercise: A shape is «enlarged by a scale factor of 3». What happens to its sides? | They change colour | *They are three times longer | They become shorter | They stay the same length
exercise: Which phrase means a photo that has been printed bigger? | A hidden photo | A torn photo | *An enlarged photo | A folded photo
test: What does the «-ed» ending in «enlarged» tell you? | It is a question | It is going to happen tomorrow | *It happened in the past | It happens every day
test: In «an enlarged heart», what does enlarged describe? | A heart that is hidden | *A heart that is bigger than normal | A heart that is very cold | A heart that has stopped
exam: Which sentence uses enlarged to mean bigger than normal because of illness? | The enlarged shape had longer sides | *The doctor said his heart was enlarged | The shop sold an enlarged photo | We enlarged the poster for the school fair
